// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO3/7/9/12-14/18/38 - dedicated GDI display
// connector signals with no general-purpose alias (DC/FCS/SDCS/BUSY_TE/
// INT/TCS/CS/RES). The shared SPI/I2C bus (SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDA/SCL)
// and GPIO21 (also GDI_BLK, but LED_BUILTIN) stay kept.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard "Boot Key"
// pushbutton, per DFRobot wiki.dfrobot.com/dfr1145/ pin table ("Boot Key
// GPIO0"). Also this chip's boot-mode strapping pin (see pinNotes).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO47 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard "User Key"
// pushbutton, per DFRobot wiki.dfrobot.com/dfr1145/ pin table ("User Key
// GPIO47", D14).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO21 (LED_BUILTIN/D13/GDI_BLK) confirmed as a plain
// onboard LED (not WS2812/NeoPixel) per wiki.dfrobot.com/dfr1145/ ("LED
// GPIO21"), but no source states active-high/active-low drive polarity -
// left untagged (no led_high/led_low) per this project's no-guess policy.
